// BowerSecurityEvents: one row per Bower security event, with delivery replays collapsed.
// Bower delivers at least once. Every replay path re-sends the stored queue row, so the
// copies share the collector-stamped (CollectorId, EventId): an ambiguous Logs Ingestion
// acknowledgement (accepted, response lost), a crash before the acknowledgement commit,
// a restored queue backup and a dead-letter replay. A source resend (RELP or TCP syslog
// after a collector restart, a WEC re-read) of a record whose queue row was lost or
// purged gets the same source-computed EventId. `bower archive replay` must go through a collector with
// the original BOWER_COLLECTOR_ID (a collector with another id refuses it), so it keeps
// the same identity too. Labels never change the identity: producers control them.
// The first copy is kept, so a later row (replayed, or sent by a producer that reused an
// EventId) never replaces content that detections already evaluated.
//   BowerFirstIngested  ingestion_time() of the first copy. Detections use it to evaluate
//                       a late event once, when it first arrived.
//   BowerLastIngested   ingestion_time() of the latest copy.
//   BowerCopies         rows that share the identity (1 = no replay).
//   BowerEventTime      the event time Bower sent. Azure Monitor rewrites TimeGenerated
//                       to the receive time when it is more than two days old; the
//                       original survives in RawEnvelope.timeGenerated.
//   BowerTimeRewritten  true when TimeGenerated no longer equals the sent event time.
// Collector health records and synthetic canaries are operational signals, not security
// events: deploy/sentinel/monitoring queries them from BowerSecurity_CL directly.
// The caller's time range still filters TimeGenerated. All copies of an event share
// TimeGenerated unless Azure rewrote it, so a range keeps or drops them together.
// Count events with count() after this function, never dcount() on the raw table:
// dcount() is an estimate.
BowerSecurity_CL
| where EventType !in ("collector_health", "collector_canary")
| extend BowerIngested = ingestion_time()
| summarize arg_min(BowerIngested, *), BowerLastIngested = max(BowerIngested), BowerCopies = count()
    by CollectorId, EventId
| project-rename BowerFirstIngested = BowerIngested
| extend BowerEventTime = coalesce(todatetime(RawEnvelope.timeGenerated), TimeGenerated)
| extend BowerTimeRewritten = BowerEventTime != TimeGenerated
